    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
      children: "Spec-driven approaches introduce upfront cost that doesn't always pay off. Writing comprehensive specifications requires time, expertise, and discipline-resources that may be scarce in fast-moving environments. For exploratory work where requirements are genuinely uncertain, extensive specifications can premature optimization. A quick prototype with loose specs might reveal fundamental issues that would have made detailed specifications wasteful. The key is calibrating specification rigor to project risk: high-stakes, well-understood problems justify detailed specs; experimental features don't."
    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
